<p>Decimal 36877. Also known as <strong>VICCRD</strong>.</p>
<p>The noise voice. Instead of a tone it produces white noise, which is what
explosions, engines, drums and footsteps are usually built from.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bit 7</strong> - switches the voice on (1) or off (0).</li>
<li><strong>Bits 6-0</strong> - the pitch of the noise: low values give a deep rumble, high
values a bright hiss.</li>
</ul>
<p>Nothing is heard while the volume in AUX_COLOR_AND_VOLUME ($900E) is 0, and
writing 0 to the register switches the voice off again.</p>

<p>Example</p>
<code>
AUX_COLOR_AND_VOLUME := 15;   // full volume
SOUNDFX_REGISTER := NOTE_C2;   // play a note
...
SOUNDFX_REGISTER := 0;         // silence this voice
</code>
<p>See also SOUND1_REGISTER, SOUND2_REGISTER, SOUND3_REGISTER and
SOUNDFX_REGISTER, and the NOTE_ constants.</p>
